1
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,960
算了，反正没有人想要吃鸡蛋
All right, so who needs eggs, anyway?

2
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,780
麦克，这是早餐
Mike, it's breakfast.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,180
爸妈需要每天补充蛋白质
Mom and Dad need all the protein they can get.

4
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:16,080
你只会让我紧张，我再试一遍
You're just making me nervous. I'll try again.

5
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,220
好啊，12次后就会成功了
Hey, why not? The 12th time's a charm.

6
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:29,980
垃圾管道也有忍耐的限度
Even garbage disposals have limits, Carol.

7
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,480
我的碟子都放不下了
I got no more room on the tray, anyway.

8
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:35,320
爸妈能饱餐一顿了
Yeah, Mom and Dad are gonna scarf this stuff up.

9
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,660
-麦片？ -有了
- All right, we got oaties? - Check.

10
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:37,880
-花生酱加面包？ -有了
- Peanut butter toast? - Check.

11
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:38,880
-土豆片？ -有了
- Space bars? - Check.

12
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:39,980
-香槟 -有了
- Champagne? - Check.

13
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:40,720
洗胃工具？
Stomach pump?

14
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:44,600
凯罗，尽管说你的风凉话
Oh, sure, sure. Go ahead and criticize, Carol.

15
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,380
我和本准备早餐时你在干什么？
But where were you when Ben and I were planning this breakfast?

16
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,300
-梳妆 -你偷懒
- Putting on my face. - You missed.

17
00:00:53,451 --> 00:00:54,600
好了
Okay.

18
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,800
我们应该开门踮脚进去
We're gonna open the door and tiptoe in without making a sound.

19
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,180
不，我们应该大叫大嚷
No. We'll scream and surprise them.

20
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:05,040
老年人受不了刺激
That could do serious harm to people their age.

21
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,080
那么你踮脚，我嚷嚷
So? You tiptoe, and I'll scream.

22
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:11,780
-本 -我喜欢嚷嚷
- Ben. - I like to scream.

23
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,320
你真走运
How lucky for you.

24
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,840
小声点，会吵醒他们的
Hey, come on, quiet down. You're gonna wake them up.

25
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:18,540
你们就不能理性一点吗？
Do I have to do all the thinking?

26
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,380
等我长大了.
Just wait till I grow bigger.

27
00:01:21,645 --> 00:01:22,960
你永远也长不大
You're not going to grow bigger, Ben.

28
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,840
爸妈那天晚上还因此哭了呢
Mom and Dad were crying about it the other night.

29
00:01:26,317 --> 00:01:28,842
好，准备好没？
All right. You guys ready?

30
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,840
结婚周年纪念快乐!
Happy anniversary!

31
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:15,940
-妈妈？ -爸爸？
- Mom? - Dad?

32
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:16,040
-奇了 -早上7点
- This is very strange. - It's 7:00 in the morning.

33
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:16,140
星期六早上，他们去哪了？
Saturday morning. Where could they be?

34
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:16,240
也许他们受够了我们，溜了
Well, maybe they finally had enough of us and moved.

35
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:16,340
这就像<阴阳魔界>那部电视剧.
You know, this is exactly like that Twilight Zone I saw.

36
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:16,440
有一对夫妻 虽然大家都觉得他们怪怪的
There was these parents who everybody thought was just a little strange.

37
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:16,540
想不到一天夜里.
And then, one dark night...

38
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:16,640
孩子们跟踪他们进入一片阴森的树林
their kids followed them into this creepy forest...

39
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:16,740
接着看到奇形怪状的飞碟
where they saw them get into this weird-looking flying saucer.

40
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:16,840
他们发现父母原来是外星人
And that's when they found out that their parents were these aliens...

41
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:16,940
来自外太空
from outer space.

42
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:17,040
孩子们
Hi, guys.

43
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:45,380
结婚纪念日快乐!
Happy anniversary?

44
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:45,480
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E19 -= The.Anniversary.That.Never.Was =- Subripped by zerox

45
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:45,580
这次准备好没？
You guys ready this time?

46
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:45,680
麦克，等等
Just a second, Mike.

47
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:45,780
-杰森？ -快点，盘子很重
- Jason? - Come on, these trays are heavy.

48
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:45,880
杰森，来吧
Jason, come on.

49
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:45,980
好的
Okay.

50
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:46,080
好了!
Ready!

51
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:46,180
结婚纪念日快乐
Happy anniversary.

52
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:48,440
真让人大吃一惊!
What a surprise!

53
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:51,200
待会看看厨房，都是垃圾.
Yeah, wait till you see the kitchen. There's garbage...

54
00:03:51,495 --> 00:03:53,120
还有惊喜呢
Now for the rest of the surprise.

55
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:56,240
为了表达我们对父母的爱.
We wanted to give you something that reflects our love for you...

56
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:59,180
为了反映我们家庭的内聚力
and the deep bond that holds this family together.

57
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,240
-所以.. -我们要出城去
- So... - We're leaving town.

58
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:08,000
仅此一天，让你们摆脱我们
Just for the day, so you can spend it alone without any of us in your hair.

59
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,120
你们就别争辩了
Now, don't give us any arguments.

60
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,460
请你们别走
Oh, please don't go.

61
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,760
你们想得真周到
Oh, that's so sweet.

62
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,020
是的，可是爸爸妈妈今天都很忙
It really is, but your mom and I have a very busy day ahead.

63
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:22,120
我们打算今晚庆祝
We really planned on celebrating tonight.

64
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:25,780
奶奶来了
Grandma's here.

65
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:28,160
是吗？
She is?

66
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:31,240
奶奶要带我们去曼哈顿看<假凤虚凰>
Yeah, Grandma's taking us to Manhattan for the matinee of La Cage Aux Folles.

67
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,840
这是本季度唯一值得观看的戏
Yeah, if there's one show you gotta see this season, this is the one.

68
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:36,960
妈妈!
Hi, Mom!

69
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,480
-真是个惊喜 -最好不过了
- Oh, guys, what a lovely surprise. - It's the best.

70
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:46,600
我约了一个病人 妈妈有篇报道要做调查
But I've got a patient to see, your mom has that story to research.

71
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,860
我们也许没时间在一起
We probably won't even have any time to spend alone.

72
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:53,040
你们犯不着冒生命的危险坐奶奶的车
So there's really no reason for you to endanger your lives in Grandma's car.

73
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,800
这份大礼要不要随便你们
You guys can use the gift or not. That's up to you.

74
00:04:56,860 --> 00:05:00,355
我可不会错过能去纽约.
But I'm not going to miss my chance to see 24 of the hottest looking babes...

75
00:05:00,420 --> 00:05:01,140
观摩那24位美女的机会
in the Big Apple.

76
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,780
我也是，不知道为什么
I'm with Mike. I have no idea why.

77
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,880
麦克，戏中那些“美女”其实是.
Mike, about these "hot babes" in the Cage Aux Folles...

78
00:05:08,505 --> 00:05:09,200
爸爸.
Dad...

79
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:13,780
我已经告诉麦克关于那场戏的所有资料
I already told Mike everything he needs to know about the show.

80
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:15,960
滴水不漏，好了吗？
Everything. Got it?

81
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,780
麦克，希望有人告诉你.
Well, Mike, I hope someone has told you...

82
00:05:18,849 --> 00:05:21,206
麦克，别忘了望远镜
Mike, don't forget your binoculars.

83
00:05:22,886 --> 00:05:24,880
真是个好妹妹
Is this a great sis, or what?

84
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:29,520
凯罗，你不知道那些妞是男人扮的？
Carol, you do know that these hot babes are really guys?

85
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:35,320
我知道，但是.
Yeah, I do, but...

86
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:40,580
我们确实可以二人世界
You know, Jason, we could actually spend the day together.

87
00:05:40,671 --> 00:05:41,820
是啊
Yeah.

88
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:44,880
遗憾的是我有一堆文案工作
Too bad I've got a mountain of paperwork to do today.

89
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,580
我也要去烫头发
I know, and I have a hair appointment...

90
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,480
还要花几个小时找资料
and several hours of research on the story I'm doing, but...

91
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,300
我可以推迟到明天
I could put those off till tomorrow.

92
00:05:52,549 --> 00:05:54,760
星期六我要更新资料
But Saturday is my day to update the files.

93
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:56,640
还约了一个病人
And I do have that patient to see.

94
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,360
说得对
Oh, you're right.

95
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:01,420
懒洋洋的，放松的，没有人打扰的.
I guess I just got distracted by the thought of...

96
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:06,300
漫长的一天，会让我分神的
a long, lazy relaxing day together, with no interruptions.

97
00:06:08,832 --> 00:06:10,291
而且
Besides...

98
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:13,040
我们一整天做些什么好？
what would we do all day?

99
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:18,540
很难说，清理浴缸吧
Oh, I don't know. We could always grout the bathtub.

100
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,340
我也可以像你一样取消工作
Well, I'll cancel my appointments if you cancel yours.

101
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:32,000
管道修理，工人今天会来修理垃圾管
The plumbing. The plumber's supposed to come by today to fix the garbage disposal.

102
00:06:32,689 --> 00:06:34,808
害我担心呢
You had me worried there.

103
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,860
亲爱的，我们该走了，订座是午餐的
Honey, we have to go. That lunch reservation is for noon.

104
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,880
亲爱的，你在干嘛？
Honey, what are you doing?

105
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:49,140
清洁工要来了，不能让她看到这么乱
The cleaning woman's coming. I can't let her see this mess.

106
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:55,240
她早晚会发现我们是大懒虫
Sooner or later, she's bound to find out we're slobs, Maggie.

107
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,420
这下在海岸餐厅订了座.
Come on. For now, we have a reservation for lunch. Rockaway Beach.

108
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,820
我们去听涛去
Watching the waves caress the shore...

109
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:06,960
美酒金樽，合卺交杯
sipping champagne from silver goblets, and toasting the woman...

110
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,560
陪伴我靠运气，才智和美貌.
I was lucky enough to find...

111
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:12,040
才能娶来的娘子
smart enough to marry, and handsome enough to keep.

112
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:16,560
杰森，你有时候还真浪漫
Oh, Jason, you can be such a romantic sometimes.

113
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,600
暂停一下
Hold that thought.

114
00:07:27,377 --> 00:07:28,427
你好
Hi.

115
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:31,020
我叫巴兹，是管道工
I'm Buzz, the plumber.

116
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:35,560
你们家垃圾通道坏了？
You got a bum garbage disposal?

117
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:39,340
我们取消了修理 你在车上没收到消息？
Gee, we cancelled that appointment. Didn't they call you in the truck?

118
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,760
车上没有对讲机
They won't let me have a radio in my truck.

119
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:46,840
我们有个约会得出去
Well, it's just that we have an appointment that we have to keep.

120
00:07:47,280 --> 00:07:50,100
那我过一会再来
I could come back later.

121
00:07:50,501 --> 00:07:51,586
谢谢
Thanks.

122
00:07:54,471 --> 00:07:55,960
-等等 -等等
- Wait. - Wait.

123
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,520
你需要多长时间
How long would it take you to fix it?

124
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,860
半小时或45分钟
Oh, half hour, 45 minutes.

125
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,980
好吧，请进来
Okay. Come in, please.

126
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,960
我打电话去改订座
I'll call and move the reservation.

127
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:20,080
巴兹，维修费用怎么算？
Buzz, how much do you charge?

128
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,540
每小时50块
$50 an hour.

129
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:28,760
喂，弗瑞德，对
Hi. Oh, hello, Fred. Yeah.

130
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:31,000
好，等等 麦姬，你的编辑
Sure, just a second. Maggie, it's your editor.

131
00:08:34,811 --> 00:08:35,820
喂？
Hello?

132
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:36,800
喂，弗瑞德
Oh, hi, Fred.

133
00:08:38,348 --> 00:08:39,398
真的？
Really?

134
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:40,800
好极了
Oh, that's great.

135
00:08:42,185 --> 00:08:43,305
今天？
Today?

136
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,879
可是我.
Oh, but l...

137
00:08:45,188 --> 00:08:47,180
当然可以
Well, sure I can.

138
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,040
好的，好的
You bet. You bet. I'll be there.

139
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,300
对，谢谢，再见
Yes. Thank you. Bye.

140
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,860
我去通知饭店
Let me call the restaurant.

141
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,520
-杰森 -借电话一用
- Jason... - Can I have the phone?

142
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:57,220
-报馆弗瑞德打来了 -我知道
- That was Fred at the paper. - I know.

143
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:03,080
他肯定是打来祝贺我们的结婚纪念
I'll bet that nut called to wish us a happy anniversary.

144
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:09,140
杰森，你是要让我内疚吧？ 因为我有个坏消息
Jason, you're just trying to make me feel guilty because you know I have bad news.

145
00:09:09,379 --> 00:09:10,400
对
Sure.

146
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:14,220
难道精神病专家也对付不了老婆？
What's the fun of being a psychiatrist if you can't play mind games on your wife?

147
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,560
亲爱的，我真的花了几个星期 才把采访定下来
Seriously, honey. I've been trying to nail down this interview for weeks...

148
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,640
可只能是今天
and it finally came through. But it's got to be today.

149
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,620
-好吧 -去华盛顿
- Okay. - In Washington.

150
00:09:22,893 --> 00:09:24,320
华盛顿？
Washington?

151
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:25,280
采访谁？
Who with?

152
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,420
知道交通部长吗？
You know the Secretary of Transportation?

153
00:09:27,931 --> 00:09:29,153
知道
Yeah.

154
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,700
我这次要采访副部长的.
I'm meeting with the third assistant to the deputy...

155
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:34,100
代言人的第三助理
of the undersecretary who reports to her.

156
00:09:36,907 --> 00:09:38,164
哇
Wow.

157
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:41,060
老实说，这是我采访过最大的人物
Oh, honestly, honey, this is the only shot I'm going to get at this.

158
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:43,720
机不可失，时不再来
- And if I don't do it now, I've lost it. - Well...

159
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,380
飞去华盛顿要45分钟
It's a 45-minute commuter flight to Washington. I can go do the interview...

160
00:09:46,380 --> 00:09:48,840
采访结束后我可以赶回来吃晚饭 我请客
and be back in time to have dinner with you. My treat.

161
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,920
若是你不满意.
But if you're disappointed...

162
00:09:52,060 --> 00:09:55,180
我会留在家，吃午饭，我也会高兴
I'll stay home, I'll have lunch, I'll be happy...

163
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,540
-我也会很满足 -如果你一定要去.
- I'll be content, totally fulfilled... - Look, if you got to go...

164
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:58,780
谢谢
Oh, thanks.

165
00:09:59,940 --> 00:10:02,140
我就知道父亲对你的看法是错误的
I knew my dad was wrong about you.

166
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:08,240
今天，我和你总会有机会.
Just so, at some point today, you and I finally get a chance...

167
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:09,880
去清理浴缸
to grout the tub.

168
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:12,440
肯定了
Count on it.

169
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:17,980
忘了带工具箱
I forgot my toolbox.

170
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,380
-再见，奶奶 -谢谢
- Bye, Grandma. See you soon. - Thanks a lot.

171
00:10:22,519 --> 00:10:23,571
谢谢，奶奶
Thanks, Grandma.

172
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:32,280
她们的裙子真漂亮
I thought the gowns were beautiful.

173
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:35,000
这部戏有关的人员都应该枪毙
I think everyone connected with that show should be shot.

174
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,400
包括你喝彩的红头发姑娘？
Even the redhead you whistled at?

175
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:40,520
好像是莫里斯
That would be Maurice.

176
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:47,180
凯罗，这个笑话不错
Okay, Carol, it was a fine joke.

177
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:49,660
是个好笑话，甚至是好笑的笑话
A good joke. Possibly even a funny joke.

178
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,180
但受罪的人是谁？
But who really paid the price here?

179
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:55,980
是我？不，是分不清真假的本
Was it me? No. It was little, confused Ben.

180
00:10:57,680 --> 00:11:01,740
莫里斯原来是爱荷华州的橄榄球员
Hey, you guys, Maurice was a tight end at Iowa State.

181
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,560
爸爸，妈妈，我们回来了
Mom, Dad? We're back.

182
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:06,660
迫不及待要告诉他们是吧？
You just can't wait to tell them, huh, Carol?

183
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:09,780
-爸爸妈妈？ -孩子们
- Mom? Dad? - Guys.

184
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,160
-今天很浪漫吧？ -不尽然
- Did you and Mom have a romantic day? - Well, not exactly.

185
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:16,180
你们小声点，我刚看完病人
Can you keep it down 'cause I'm just finishing up with a patient in here.

186
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,100
-好的 -妈妈在哪？
- Sure. - Hey, where's Mom?

187
00:11:18,842 --> 00:11:20,031
华盛顿
Washington.

188
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,520
华盛顿？情况不妙
Washington? This is not a good sign.

189
00:11:29,019 --> 00:11:31,860
也许是他们独处时，爸爸开起玩笑来
Hey, I bet when Mom and Dad got alone, Dad started telling his jokes...

190
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,420
妈妈就跳上飞机逃走了
and Mom hopped the first plane to anywhere.

191
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,840
麦克，有个死人躺在厨房里
Mike, there's a body on the kitchen floor.

192
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:40,040
男的女的？
Man or woman?

193
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,400
我再也分不清了
I can't tell anymore.

194
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,980
去看看是什么人
Somebody should go check him out.

195
00:11:49,873 --> 00:11:51,028
本
Ben.

196
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:54,500
糟了，我的鸡汤
Look out. My chicken sauce.

197
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,520
-爸爸，你没看到.. -还好
- Dad, did you see... - Oh, good.

198
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:58,900
-没粘锅底 -爸，你没看到.
- It didn't stick. - Dad, you notice there's a...

199
00:11:59,149 --> 00:12:01,660
-<假凤虚凰>好看吗？ -好看
- So, how was Cage Aux Folles? - Great.

200
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:04,060
莫里斯还在剧团里？
Is Maurice still with the show?

201
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,940
-莫里斯 -你俩闭嘴
- Maurice. - Shut up, both of you.

202
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:12,640
-巴兹，怎样了？ -快修完了
- Buzz, how's it going? - Almost finished.

203
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:17,680
才修了5个半小时，1小时才50块
Only five and a half hours at $50 an hour.

204
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,400
爸，妈妈还回来吗？
Dad, is Mom ever coming back?

205
00:12:20,660 --> 00:12:23,940
她说会赶回来烛光晚餐
She'll be back in plenty of time for our candlelit dinner for two.

206
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,880
晚上你们去奶奶家好吗？
You guys will spend the night at Grandma's, okay?

207
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:33,100
我们一天冒了几次生命危险了
Oh, come on, Dad. How many times do we have to risk our lives in a single day?

208
00:12:34,251 --> 00:12:35,339
喂？
Hello?

209
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:38,540
亲爱的，非常非常对不起 我还在华盛顿
Oh, sweetheart. I am so, so sorry. I'm still in Washington.

210
00:12:38,820 --> 00:12:40,280
一切都搞砸了
Everything got screwed up on this end...

211
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,740
采访推迟到明早
and the interview got put off until tomorrow...

212
00:12:41,958 --> 00:12:44,184
今晚报馆让我在黄金饭店过夜
so the paper is putting me up at the Hotel Royale tonight.

213
00:12:44,194 --> 00:12:45,800
明天一早就去采访
I'll interview him first thing in the morning.

214
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,400
然后我尽快赶回来庆祝咱的周年纪念
Then I'll get home as fast as I can to celebrate our anniversary...

215
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,000
真的，亲爱的，早知道这种情况.
because, I swear, honey, if I'd known this was gonna happen...

216
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,420
我就不会来了
I never would have come.

217
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,460
你是谁？
Who is this?

218
00:12:56,206 --> 00:12:57,602
杰森
Jason.

219
00:13:03,747 --> 00:13:05,506
修好了
All done.

220
00:13:06,850 --> 00:13:08,347
好极了
Wonderful.

221
00:13:08,785 --> 00:13:09,839
那.
So...

222
00:13:09,853 --> 00:13:11,943
把帐单寄\给我吧
I guess you'll be sending me a bill on that.

223
00:13:11,955 --> 00:13:14,250
特级邮递
Posthaste.

224
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,080
修理费总共多少？
How much will it come to?

225
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:19,200
劳务费加上.
Well, I have to add the labor...

226
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,200
-配件.. -大约多少？
- and the parts... - Ballpark?

227
00:13:21,565 --> 00:13:21,630
347.75

228
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:25,964
$347.75.

229
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,620
好奇问句.
Just out of curiosity...

230
00:13:29,760 --> 00:13:32,200
换个新的要多少钱？
how much would a new garbage disposal cost me?

231
00:13:34,244 --> 00:13:35,298
好
Perfect.

232
00:13:35,712 --> 00:13:37,960
你要换一个新的？
Would you like me to install one?

233
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,780
不，不，谢谢
No, no. No, thank you.

234
00:13:40,750 --> 00:13:41,907
再见
Bye.

235
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:43,760
周年纪念快乐
Happy anniversary.

236
00:13:47,040 --> 00:13:49,040
爸爸，这些垃圾你不吃了？
Hey, Dad, you gonna eat anymore of this junk on your plate?

237
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:51,580
-不，我不饿 -麦克.
- Nah, I'm not hungry. - Michael...

238
00:13:52,128 --> 00:13:53,455
这叫鸡肉
it's fowl.

239
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:54,340
还真不知道
Tell me about it.

240
00:13:55,665 --> 00:13:56,754
爸爸
Dad?

241
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:58,120
对不起，我没听见
Sorry, I wasn't listening.

242
00:13:58,780 --> 00:14:00,620
可是你看上去是在听
Looked like you were. I guess you psychiatrists...

243
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:04,100
一直跟疯子打交道 练出一身装听的本事
get pretty used to faking it after all those years of listening to wackos.

244
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:08,240
“疯子”两个字对精神病医生来说.
Michael, "wacko" is a term psychiatrists reserve...

245
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,320
只能用在家人身上
for members of their immediate family.

246
00:14:11,681 --> 00:14:13,873
-我说着玩的 -不要说着玩
- I'm just kidding. - Well, don't.

247
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:21,680
刚才所见乃经典的泄愤行为.
What you've just witnessed is a classic display of displaced anger...

248
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:24,220
我把一腔的怒气.
in which I allowed my frustrations to be vented...

249
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:26,600
发泄在第一个惹我的人身上
on the first available person to upset me.

250
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:29,940
这种行为缓解了我的精神压力
This transference lets me lessen my stress...

251
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,660
使我感到..自己很傻
and allows me to feel really stupid.

252
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,860
你不能就这样坐上飞机，一走了之
You can't get on that plane and leave.

253
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:41,800
-你爱的是我，你很清楚 -不，我爱的是拉里
- It's me you love. You know it is. - No, no, Curly. It's Larry.

254
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:45,540
-我一直爱着拉里 -可是你对我说的那些话.
- It's always been Larry. - But all those things you said.

255
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:48,060
是我弄错了，对不起
I was mistaken. I'm sorry, Curly.

256
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:49,420
我要跟拉里在一起
But my place is with Larry.

257
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,600
我不能留在这当你的陪亲
I can't stay here and be your stooge.

258
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:55,480
我会不择手段留住你
I'll do whatever I have to do to stop you.

259
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:58,380
我决不会让你上飞机
I'm not letting you get on that plane.

260
00:15:02,165 --> 00:15:04,597
你当初就不该上飞机
You shouldn't have gotten on the plane.

261
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,500
对，722房西弗小姐
Yes, this is Mrs. Seaver in 722.

262
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:18,700
请帮我订一张飞机票
Is there anyone in the hotel that can help me with plane reservations?

263
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:27,740
有什么办法能让爸爸高兴起来？
I wish there was something we could do to cheer Dad up.

264
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:28,860
你离开家就行了
You could leave home.

265
00:15:30,100 --> 00:15:33,440
-我有个主意 -麦克，爸爸是.
- I got an idea. - Mike, Dad's been deeply disappointed...

266
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,080
为了爱而失落
by the woman he loves.

267
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:39,300
经过莫里斯这一次，你肯定能体会
I'm sure you can understand that after Maurice.

268
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:43,960
-我这个是好主意 -失落是因为生了你
- It's a really good idea. - He's used to disappointment, Carol.

269
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,400
毕竟第一个孩子是你
After all, his second-oldest child is you.

270
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:49,580
不要太敏感了好不好？
You're really Mr. Sensitivity, you know?

271
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:54,140
这不止是一顿晚餐
It's not the dinner. It's just that...

272
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:57,780
他们需要在这个特别的日子.
they need at least a moment in that special day when...

273
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:01,400
情深地看着对方.
they can be together and look into each other's eyes...

274
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:03,960
回首过去走过的路
and think about the years they've shared.

275
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:07,520
幸福的岁月，艰难的岁月
The good times, the bad times.

276
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,220
他们要学戏里面的人？
You mean they want to "Do Wah Diddy"?

277
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,020
这20块是谁丢的？
Hey, who lost $20?

278
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:15,440
-什么？ -在哪？
- What? - Where?

279
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:18,420
这样你们就注意我了
Now that I have your attention...

280
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,480
爸爸干嘛不飞到华盛顿见妈妈？
why doesn't Dad fly to Washington and be with Mom tonight?

281
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:26,960
真气人，又被他想出来了
I hate it when he does that.

282
00:16:29,085 --> 00:16:30,560
我去收拾行李
I'll pack him a bag.

283
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:32,080
我去订机票
I'll order the plane tickets.

284
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:35,240
一如既往，有功无赏
And I'll get no credit, as usual.

285
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:40,600
沃拉先生的自卑感.
And Mr. Walla is showing great improvement...

286
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,140
得到了很大的改善
in controlling his feelings of inadequacy.

287
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:46,420
心理治疗最大的用处是.
The sessions are proving especially useful...

288
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:48,660
减少结婚纪念日
in decreasing his anniversary.

289
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:52,320
删除“结婚纪念日”，口误
Ignore "anniversary." Freudian slip.

290
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,340
-减少焦虑 -爸爸
- In decreasing his anxiety. - Dad?

291
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:58,760
我在工作，删掉“我在工作”，儿子打扰
I'm working. Ignore "I'm working." Teenage son.

292
00:16:59,516 --> 00:17:00,948
爸爸？
Dad?

293
00:17:00,950 --> 00:17:04,214
我要关掉录音，不然在法庭上.
I'm turning the recorder off now, so as not to have it used against me...

294
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,220
这会对我不利
in a court of law.

295
00:17:05,955 --> 00:17:08,013
什么事这么重要!
Mike, this better be important.

296
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:11,740
我代表大家说句，你走吧
Dad, on behalf of all of us, get out.

297
00:17:14,040 --> 00:17:15,520
怎么了？
What's going on?

298
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,740
现在是你儿子跟你谈话
Come on, this is your son you're talking to here.

299
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:21,280
我察觉到今年的纪念日.
Now, I'm sensitive enough to know that this anniversary thing...

300
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,660
让你痛不欲生
has you feeling like garbage.

301
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:26,040
你直接刺他一刀好了
Why don't you just shoot him?

302
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:29,880
在你们伤害我以前.
Well, before anyone shoots me or shoves me down the garbage disposal...

303
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,480
而且这样也徒劳无功.
which probably doesn't work anyway...

304
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:35,380
我想知道为什么要走？ 为什么是本开车？
would you please explain to me where we're going? And why is Ben driving?

305
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:36,140
Well...

306
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:39,520
我想出来你应该飞去华盛顿 让妈妈吃一惊
I decided you should fly to Washington tonight and surprise Mom.

307
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,420
你想出来？
You decided?

308
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,740
这个主意不错，可是.
Well, that's a great idea, but l...

309
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:48,540
行李收拾好了，机票订了 奶奶正在赶过来
Dad, your bag's packed, your ticket's ordered, and Grandma's on her way over.

310
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:52,580
这个主意太好了，可是.
Oh, hey, look, that's wonderful, but I can't...

311
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:54,780
我就不能再留下了
stay here another second.

312
00:17:55,872 --> 00:17:57,600
-爸爸，再见 -再见
- Bye, Dad. Bye-bye. - See you later.

313
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:01,700
“我解决了问题”？ “我想出来你应该飞去华盛顿”？
"I solved your problem?" "I decided you should fly to Washington?"

314
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:04,160
管他是谁的主意？你还小
Who cares whose idea it was? Grow up.

315
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:06,820
对，别老自以为是
Yeah. Stop thinking of yourself.

316
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:10,700
奶奶来了
Here comes Grandma.

317
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:14,140
不是奶奶，开这么慢
It's not Grandma. It's not going fast enough.

318
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,060
而且没有开到路中间
It's staying on the right side of the road.

319
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:18,553
-天哪.. -不是吧
- Holy... - Oh, no.

320
00:18:18,561 --> 00:18:20,187
难以置信
I don't believe it.

321
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,100
-孩子们 -妈妈
- Hi, guys. - Hi, Mom.

322
00:18:22,732 --> 00:18:25,291
-爸爸在客厅里吗？ -不在
- Oh, is your dad in the living room? - No.

323
00:18:25,301 --> 00:18:27,360
很好，我要让他吃一惊
Good. I want to surprise him.

324
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:28,980
肯定会大吃一惊
And I think you will, too.

325
00:18:33,676 --> 00:18:36,577
-在厨房？ -不
- Is he in the kitchen? - No.

326
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:38,580
-睡房？ -不
- In the bedroom? - No.

327
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,720
-他在哪？ -华盛顿
- Well, where is he? - Washington.

328
00:18:43,753 --> 00:18:44,800
什么？
What?

329
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:47,560
我也不清楚，只知道是本的主意
I don't get it either. All I know is, it was Ben's idea.

330
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:53,780
飞往华盛顿的256航机马上就要起飞了
Attention. Final boarding, flight 256 for Washington National.

331
00:18:53,863 --> 00:18:54,920
27号门
Gate 27.

332
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,880
旁边的座位没人，可以坐过去.
Maybe that aisle seat isn't taken if you wanted to slide over...

333
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:11,100
让大家多点空间.
then we'd both have more room to...

334
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:12,840
这是L排2座
No. This is Row L, Seat 2.

335
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:15,660
我的座位，风雨不改
This is my seat. All flights, any flight.

336
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:16,760
这是我的座位
My seat.

337
00:19:19,088 --> 00:19:20,589
好吧
Okay.

338
00:19:31,060 --> 00:19:32,200
借过
Excuse me.

339
00:19:32,368 --> 00:19:36,060
-麻烦你.. -不行，这是L排2座，我的座位
- Do you mind if... - No. This is Row L, Seat 2. This is my seat.

340
00:19:36,060 --> 00:19:38,540
风雨不改
All flights, any flight. My seat.

341
00:19:40,243 --> 00:19:41,574
好吧
Okay.

342
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:45,980
-杰森.. -不，我叫路德
- Jason? - No. Luther.

343
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:51,560
我在跟他说话，亲爱的？
I'm talking to him. Honey?

344
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:58,720
-麦姬，怎么到这了？ -我想你
- Maggie. What are you doing here? - I missed you.

345
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:01,680
-我也想你 -太好了
- I missed you, too. - That's sweet.

346
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:04,280
你那个迫不及待的采访怎样了？
What about that big interview that couldn't wait?

347
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,660
我问自己，电视上的泰德.
Well, I asked myself what Ted Koppel would do...

348
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:10,300
若能嫁给你这种好男人，他会怎么做？
if he were married to a wonderful man like you.

349
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:14,260
首先是别让丈夫日夜操劳
Well, first of all, I wouldn't let him work that late every night.

350
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:17,500
今晚我应该陪我的大人物.
I figured I could fly back tomorrow to do the interview...

351
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:20,380
明早再飞回去采访
after I spend the evening with my main squeeze.

352
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,040
这么巧？
What a coincidence.

353
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:25,460
-你要去见什么人？ -一个非常特殊的人
- You're on your way to see someone, too? - Someone very special.

354
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,780
杰森.
Oh, Jason.

355
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:29,600
这个主意是你想出来的吗？
Did you think of this all by yourself?

356
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:32,980
这还多亏了你的另外几个男人.
Well, I got some help from the other men in your life...

357
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:35,900
麦克，本还有凯罗
Mike and Ben. And, not to mention Carol.

358
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,460
这是送给你的
Oh, look what I got for you. Look, these.

359
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:44,440
-玫瑰 -好
- Roses. - Yes.

360
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:47,560
亲爱的，真漂亮
Oh, honey, they're beautiful.

361
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:51,100
-我也有东西送你 -是吗？
- Oh, and I have something for you, too. - Yeah?

362
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:54,580
先生，谢谢
Sir? Thank you.

363
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:00,880
-对不起，你挡住我了 -对不起
- Excuse me. I can't see. - Oh, sorry.

364
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:05,760
亲爱的，我父亲没看错你
Oh, honey, my dad was right about you.

365
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:11,120
两个人度过了17个年头.
You know, when two people spend 17 years together...

366
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,580
我帮你吧
Can I help you with that?

367
00:21:12,869 --> 00:21:14,099
好的
Sure.

368
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:20,920
17年值得我们二人.
I think 17 years deserves a moment alone together...

369
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:22,440
好好庆祝一下
just the two of us.

370
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,240
我们三人.
The three of us.

371
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:28,880
我们能情深款款地看着对方说.
So that we can stare into each other's eyes and say:

372
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,160
“若是可以重来..”
"If I had it to do over..."

373
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:33,700
“我还是会兴你度过这一切，我爱你”
Oh, honey, I'd do it all over again. I love you.

374
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:34,860
我也爱你
Oh, I love you, too.

375
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:41,200
我爱你们
And I love both of you.

376
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,520
-敬爱情 -敬爱情
- To love. - To love.

377
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:58,520
-我过得很愉快 -我过得很快乐
- I had a great time. - I had a wonderful time.

378
00:22:00,283 --> 00:22:04,380
慢着，我希望再停留一秒钟
Wait. I just want it to last a moment longer.

379
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:08,820
不要再细数过去的事了
Well, then, let's not come back and say we did.

380
00:22:10,140 --> 00:22:11,500
很好，但不了
Tempting, but no.

381
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,760
我们要回到孩子们身边
We have to get back to those three beautiful children...

382
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:15,660
他们想念我们，需要我们
who miss us and need us.

383
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:17,600
你这混蛋!
You little weasel!

384
00:22:18,701 --> 00:22:19,932
嗨
Oh, hi.

385
00:22:20,020 --> 00:22:22,080
-你死定了!嗨 -嗨
- You're a dead man, Ben! Hi. - Hi.

386
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:25,640
爱船返航了，待会见
Ooh, la, la. The Love Boat's in. Hey, I'll see you later, guys.

387
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,960
麦姬，知道我在想什么吗？
Maggie, are you thinking what I'm thinking?

388
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:34,980
-想什么？ -我想起了约吉.贝拉
- What are you thinking? - I'm thinking about Yogi Berra.

389
00:22:35,551 --> 00:22:40,457
-这么巧 -他说过这么一句话.
- What a coincidence. - Well, it was Yogi who coined the phrase:

390
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:42,260
“没完的事情还没完”
"It ain't over till it's over."

391
00:23:29,071 --> 00:23:30,057
